From: RowanOS integration <rowanos@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: import real DMA heap memory for D16 linear scanout

The verified D16 Mali ICD advertises IMPORTABLE but not EXPORTABLE for
AR24/AB24 DMA-BUF images. Query the exact linear image usages and views
before selecting an import-only route. Allocate a real system DMA heap
buffer, intersect its memory types with the image requirements and import
a duplicate FD with dedicated image memory. Keep the original FD for KMS.

Use the driver's actual linear subresource offset and stride, reject
out-of-bounds layouts, and retain the existing DRM framebuffer check.
Restrict this route to verified D16 identity and packed 32-bit SDR formats;
do not relax an export capability check or invent a modifier.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [D16 vendor Mali ICD integration]
